<title>ARGENTINA: YPF makes Venezuela oil find.</title>
<headline>YPF makes Venezuela oil find.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A joint-venture between Maxus Venezuela, a subsidiary of Argentina's YPF SA and Lagoven, a subsidiary of Petroleos de Venezuela SA, has struck oil in eastern Venezuela, YPF said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Consorcio Quiriquire joint venture made the discovery in the San Luis Lagoven-1X deposit in the Quiriquire block.</p>
<p>Well tests produced 700 barrels of oil per day (bpd) in the San Antonio formation, and 1,900 bpd in the San Juan formation.</p>
<p>Maxus Venezuela has a 50 percent share in the Quiriquire block.</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
